<v CRAMER>What was it called?

1727
01:30:03.100 --> 01:30:04.000
<v MCKEE>Mr. Dave Lyons.

1728
01:30:04.000 --> 01:30:06.100
What Uncle Dave called his place, Mama?

1729
01:30:06.100 --> 01:30:06.400
<v GORDWIN>Lyons.

1730
01:30:06.400 --> 01:30:07.000
Just Lyons.

1731
01:30:07.000 --> 01:30:08.800
<v MCKEE>Right here when you turn in.

1732
01:30:08.800 --> 01:30:09.100
<v CRAMER>Oh!

1733
01:30:09.100 --> 01:30:10.300
With the Lyons Avenue . . .

1734
01:30:10.300 --> 01:30:10.600
<v GORDWIN>Yes.

1735
01:30:10.600 --> 01:30:16.000
And further down . . . Now, when I was a little girl they had one down [by] Blunt’s grandmother.

1736
01:30:16.000 --> 01:30:17.026
<v MCKEE>What was the name?

1737
01:30:17.026 --> 01:30:18.051
<v GORDWIN>The Dew Drop Inn.

1738
01:30:18.051 --> 01:30:19.077
<v MCKEE>The Dew Drop Inn?

1739
01:30:19.077 --> 01:30:19.333
<v GORDWIN>Yeah.

1740
01:30:19.333 --> 01:30:20.872
<v MCKEE>That was the name of it.

1741
01:30:20.872 --> 01:30:22.410
<v CH. GORDWIN>That's what we named this house.

1742
01:30:22.410 --> 01:30:24.462
<v GORDWIN>The name of it the Dew Drop Inn.

1743
01:30:24.462 --> 01:30:24.718
<v MCKEE>Okay.

1744
